label Choice 2.4-B1A Challenge
You cup your hand to your mouth and shout a challenge.\
\
You\: Halt, who goes there?
The men respond but as they are still some distance away, you can’t quite hear them.
- Repeat the Challenge
	set {chosen_path} = "Choice 2.4-B1AA"
- Wait for them to get closer
	set {chosen_path} = "Choice 2.4-B1B1"
[end_timeline]
label 2.4-B1AA Repeat Challenge
You steady yourself and repeat the challenge. Everything is now quiet so you focus your periscope on the area. For a second you think that maybe a bird or something flew into view, but then register the dull sound of something falling onto the duckboards behind you.
Instantly you realize the danger but it’s too late - the enemy grenade explodes, killing both you and the sentry.\
\
The End
set {chosen_path} = "Death11"
[end_timeline]
label 2.4-B1B1 Wait for them to get closer
Knowing that they are too far away, you decide to wait and keep a sharp eye on them. Since people move slowly in No Man’s Land, it takes about 20 minutes before they are in range.
You\: “Halt, who goes there?”\
\
Voice\: “We are tommies.”
Sentry\: “They're on our side.”\
\
You ignore the sentry and instead ask\:
You\: “What’s the password?”\
\
Voice\: “Please, we needing help.”
The other sentry nudges you.\
\
Sentry\: “I’m going to help.”
- Go with the Sentry
	set {chosen_path} = "Choice 2.4-B1BA"
- Stop him.
	set {chosen_path} = "Choice 2.4-B1BB"
[end_timeline]
label 2.4-B1BA
You and the sentry both ready your gear and clammer out of the trench to help the wounded men and bring them to the safety of your trench. You slither into No Man’s Land and work your way to their position.
Eventually, you make it into their crater. Rough hands grab you and the sentry, cupping your mouths as bayonets plunge into your body. Too late do you realize that they are German soldiers.  \
\
The End
set {chosen_path} = "Death12"
[end_timeline]
label 2.4-B1BB
You grab the sentry and keep him from moving.
You\: No, they don’t know the password and didn’t you notice their accent? \
\
Sentry\: What?
You shake your head and then say.\
\
You\: “Hold tight, we’ll come and help.”
Pulling the sentry closer, you whisper in his ear and instruct him to inform the Sgt that enemy soldiers are nearby.
He nods and slips off while you keep a watch on the enemy. Moments later, the sentry returns along with Sgt Fitzgerald, Cpl Barron, and 2Lt Holmes, the latter holding a flare gun in his hands.
2Lt Holmes\: “You’ve got something?”
You\: “Yes Sir, enemy soldiers about fifteen yards in front of us in a crater. They failed the challenge and have a less than convincing accent. I told them to hold tight and that we were coming to help.”
Sgt Fitzgerald gives a broad smile.\
\
2Lt Holmes\: “Let’s say we help them see where they’re going, shall we?”
As Holmes loads the flare gun, Fitzgerald has you, the sentry, and Cpl Barron prepare yourselves.You stash the periscope and grasp your rifle in your hands.
Sgt Fitzgerald\: “Fix bayonets, just in case.”
You reach down to your left hip where, between some ammunition pouches, you grab the hilt of the dagger and pull it out of its frog. A 17-inch blade is an intimidating looking weapon, especially when it’s attached to the muzzle of your Lee-Enfield.
The bayonet clicks securely into place. You then work the rifle’s action, grabbing the bolt and chambering a round, and then join the others on the fire step, weapons held at the ready. 
2Lt Holmes takes aim with the flaregun, pointing it up towards the sky above No Man’s Land, and pulls the trigger.
A distinct ‘PLOOP’ sound rings out, followed by a ‘SWOOSH’ as the projectile launches into the air, detonating with a muffled bang.
All of you bring your rifles to bear over the parapet. 
- Fire your rifle
	set {chosen_path} = "2.4-B1BB-1"
- Wait
	set {chosen_path} = "2.4-B1BB-2"
[end_timeline]
label 2.4-B1BB-1
You scan the area, now brightly illuminated by the white phosphorus burning overhead. You can see five German Soldiers in a trench.
You focus your sights on the nearest enemy and open fire, work the action, and take aim at the next. With everyone else firing beside you it’s all over in a matter of seconds.
2Lt Holmes\: Good work Private. \
\
Sgt Fitizgerald gives you an approving nod and both men head off. Cpl Barron stays with you until your watch is over.
set {chosen_path} = "3.1A2"
[end_timeline]
label 2.4-B1BB-2
You scan the area, now brightly illuminated by the white phosphorus burning overhead. You can see five German Soldiers in a trench.
You wait, and in that moment of hesitation, the enemy opens fire. A bullet strikes you in the head, killing you instantly.\
\
The End
